{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>A laughingstock to his fellow</b> — I sat as a man who was a laughingstock to his fellow, and it is like 'a laughingstock to his fellow.' And the wonder is that this one who has become a laughingstock calls to El and He answers him."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The Hebrew repeats the phrase שחוק לרעהו three times with slight syntactic variation; the hyper-literal repetition is preserved as the argument itself turns on the repeated wording."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:25.607128014Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}